South Korea ordered internet providers to block Polymarket

Korea's media and communications commission ruled that the prediction market facilitates gambling under the Criminal Act and amounts to sports betting under the National Sports Promotion Act.

@Polymarket had argued its non-custodial contracts leave it without an organizer, and that it removed Korean-language service and does not accept won. Around 30 countries, including France and Australia, already restrict access.

